    <!-- Off-schedule reason prompts (#586, product ADR-0030; late-direction option set amended by
         #649, product ADR-0033) — two options per prompt, phrased the way a user would say them; the
         answer alone decides whether the model learns. The option *set*, not just the wording, now
         differs by direction: the late direction never offers a shorten attribution. -->
    <!-- #652 round 2: shared label for the liquid-fertilizer combined action, used both by the Water
         tab's second button (CombinedWaterFertilizeActionRow) and the Fertilize tab's button when
         the plant uses liquid fertilizer (FertilizeDueActionRow). -->
    <string name="water_fertilize_combined_button">Water + Fertilize</string>
    <!-- Off-schedule reason prompts (#586, product ADR-0030) — two options per prompt, phrased the
         way a user would say them; the answer alone decides whether the model learns. -->
    <!-- Early variant: the gap is still short of the interval, so "Why now?" reads naturally. -->
    <string name="water_reason_question">Why now?</string>
    <string name="water_reason_plant_needed_it">The plant needed it</string>
    <string name="water_reason_just_my_timing">Just my schedule</string>
    <!-- Late variant (PlantCareStatus.isWateringGapLong): "Why now?" reads as an accusation on an
         overdue plant, so this asks "why was it late" instead. The plant-attribution answer here is a
         genuinely different reason — WateringReason.SOIL_STILL_MOIST — since a late gap can never
         shorten the interval (#649); phrased as its own full clause ("Soil was still moist") rather
         than reusing reschedule_reason_soil_still_moist's shorter label verbatim, since it needs to
         read as a direct answer to "Why was it late?", not a button label. Only "just my timing" is
         shared with the early variant, and even it is reworded: "just my timing" implies a choice
         that forgetting never involves, so forgetting is named outright instead. -->
    <string name="water_reason_question_late">Why was it late?</string>
    <string name="water_reason_soil_still_moist_late">Soil was still moist</string>
